  "content": {
    "id": "p55-q11-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "11",
    "prompt": "Describe the transformations to $y=x^3$ in the correct order if the transformed function has equation:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p55-q11-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$y=(x-1)^3+7$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Translate 1 unit right, then 7 units up.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}y-7&=(x-1)^3\\\\y-7&=f(x-1)\\end{aligned}$$\nTranslate 1 unit right, then 7 units up. The horizontal and vertical translations may also be applied in the opposite order.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p55-q11-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$y=4x^3-1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Dilate vertically by factor 4, then translate 1 unit down.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y+1}{4}&=x^3\\\\\\frac{y+1}{4}&=f(x)\\end{aligned}$$\nDilate vertically by factor 4, then translate 1 unit down.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p55-q11-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$y=-5x^3-3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Dilate vertically by factor 5, reflect in the $x$-axis, then translate 3 units down.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y+3}{-5}&=x^3\\\\\\frac{y+3}{-5}&=f(x)\\end{aligned}$$\nDilate vertically by factor 5, reflect in the $x$-axis, then translate 3 units down. The dilation and reflection may be interchanged.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p55-q11-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$y=2(x+7)^3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Dilate vertically by factor 2, then translate 7 units left.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{2}&=(x+7)^3\\\\\\frac{y}{2}&=f(x+7)\\end{aligned}$$\nDilate vertically by factor 2, then translate 7 units left. These vertical and horizontal transformations may also be applied in the opposite order.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p55-q11-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$y=6(2x-4)^3+5$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Dilate horizontally by factor $\\frac12$ and vertically by factor 6, then translate 2 units right and 5 units up.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}y&=6[2(x-2)]^3+5\\\\\\frac{y-5}{6}&=[2(x-2)]^3\\\\\\frac{y-5}{6}&=f(2(x-2))\\end{aligned}$$\nDilate horizontally by factor $\\frac12$, dilate vertically by factor 6, translate 2 units right, then translate 5 units up. Each dilation precedes the translation in the same direction.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      },
      {
        "id": "p55-q11-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$y=2(3x+9)^3-10$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Dilate horizontally by factor $\\frac13$ and vertically by factor 2, then translate 3 units left and 10 units down.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}y&=2[3(x+3)]^3-10\\\\\\frac{y+10}{2}&=[3(x+3)]^3\\\\\\frac{y+10}{2}&=f(3(x+3))\\end{aligned}$$\nDilate horizontally by factor $\\frac13$, dilate vertically by factor 2, translate 3 units left, then translate 10 units down. Each dilation precedes the translation in the same direction.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      }
    ]
  },
